Pacing: the in-flight capture term (unseenCaptureWorkMs) plus the three 2026-09-04 follow-ups.

Set aside on 2026-09-04 so the backlog-clock rebase change could be measured separately.
Base commit: 8d5e55d  ("Stop halving the queue growth with the deficit")
Design document: PacingInFlightHandoff.md  (sections 4-6 describe exactly this diff)
Status when set aside: never compiled, never measured on device.

Re-apply with a three-way merge, not a plain apply. Measured on 2026-09-04 against the
backlog-clock change that replaced this in the tree: seven of the eight files apply cleanly, and
CaptureAvailablePacer.kt conflicts once - where this patch's setCaptureDeadlineMs and snapshot
hunks meet that change's endDraftSequence and cancelDraftSequence.

    git add -A && git apply -3 patches/pacing-inflight-term.patch

"git apply -3" needs the index to match the worktree, so commit or stage first, or it stops at
"does not match index" before merging anything. "git stash apply" is the equivalent route.

An identical copy is in the stash entry made at the same moment (git stash list), verified byte
for byte against this file.

